Generate a consistent family of Urkaaaz Loadout spell-card illustrations.
Use the attached user-provided Loadout screenshot as the visual reference for
the card artwork's painterly fantasy quality, contrast, warm highlights, and
rich but readable materials. The screenshot's spell names and depicted effects
are not Urkaaaz content; use only the spell concepts listed here.

Run one separate image-generation request for each numbered output below,
using the same visual reference and prompt each time. Each request must produce
only its one named PNG; do not ask the image generator to return an 11-image
grid or montage.

THEMATICS

- Each illustration represents exactly one existing Urkaaaz `SpellType`.
- The art is a static selection-card illustration. It does not depict a new
  gameplay rule, spell activation sequence, UI, or status badge.
- Keep spell effects recognizable at small card size, with one clear focal
  subject and a simple background.
- Keep faction/unit silhouettes consistent with the supplied Urkaaaz unit
  images when they are provided. Do not design new unit classes.

VISUAL STYLE

- Match the attached Loadout reference's polished painterly fantasy-game
  direction: dimensional hand-painted forms, warm cinematic lighting,
  saturated but controlled magical effects, dark readable edges, and
  restrained gold/brass accents.
- Keep the artwork cohesive in camera distance, contrast, detail density, and
  palette across all spells.
- Landscape 4:3 composition. Center the main symbol/effect and leave the
  outermost 8% visually quiet so Android card cropping does not hide the
  subject.
- Full-bleed image to all canvas edges. The card frame, selection border,
  title, cost, lock, and stock indicators are rendered by Android and must not
  appear in these images.
- The screenshot is a style reference, not a request to copy its exact spell
  pictures or fictional game content.

HUMOROUS ACCENTS

- No added joke or text. Keep the existing Urkaaaz playful-fantasy tone through
  expressive but non-comedic details only; gameplay meaning takes priority.

REFERENCE IMAGE INPUT

- Use the attached user-provided Loadout screenshot for visual direction only.
- When available, use existing Urkaaaz unit icon/sprite images as references
  for recognizable allied or enemy silhouettes.
- Do not copy the screenshot's FIRE STRIKE, WIND BLAST, or EARTH SHIELD art.
- Do not create any art for invented unit or ammunition names.

OUTPUT FILES

Across the 11 separate requests, export exactly these 11 independent PNGs.
Each is a separate 512 x 384 image; never combine them into a contact sheet,
atlas, collage, or sprite sheet.

1. `loadout_spell_ice_trap.png` — `ICE_TRAP`: an icy rune trap emerging from
   battlefield soil, with sharp blue-white crystals and a clear ground-snare
   silhouette.
2. `loadout_spell_runic_bastion.png` — `RUNIC_BASTION`: a sturdy runic stone
   barrier/gate placed on a battlefield, with readable protective runes.
3. `loadout_spell_haste.png` — `HASTE`: recognizable allied units moving
   forward with concise golden wind trails, communicating increased speed.
4. `loadout_spell_heal.png` — `HEAL`: wounded allied units receiving warm
   restorative light; communicate healing, not resurrection.
5. `loadout_spell_fortress_shield.png` — `FORTRESS_SHIELD`: a fortress under
   a translucent protective shield, with the fortress clearly the focal point.
6. `loadout_spell_catapult_lock.png` — `CATAPULT_LOCK`: an enemy catapult
   restrained by visible magical runes or chains; no damage or destruction.
7. `loadout_spell_slowing_field.png` — `SLOWING_FIELD`: an enemy group moving
   through a cool-colored field that visibly impedes their movement.
8. `loadout_spell_vampiric_banner.png` — `VAMPIRIC_BANNER`: a dark crimson
   allied banner with subtle red energy returning from combat to wounded
   allies; avoid gore.
9. `loadout_spell_stone_skin.png` — `STONE_SKIN`: an allied unit protected
   by a readable layer of stone plates, communicating defense and weight.
10. `loadout_spell_siege_frenzy.png` — `SIEGE_FRENZY`: allied fighters with a
    red-gold battle surge and stronger attack posture; no new unit design.
11. `loadout_spell_berserker.png` — `BERSERKER`: the existing Defender unit
    empowered by a restrained crimson aura; use the supplied Defender art as
    the identity reference and do not depict a different unit.

Stage/archive destination before approval:
`assets_src/loadout/spell-cards/`

Android runtime destination after validation and approval:
`android-app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/`

MUST-HAVE

- Exactly one spell concept per generation request, matching its exact
  filename and `SpellType` above.
- PNG format, exact 512 x 384 dimensions, full-bleed 4:3 artwork.
- Distinct focal art, readable when shown in a small mobile card.
- No lettering, words, numbers, UI, card borders, selection glows, locks,
  coins, inventory markers, logo, watermark, or signature.
- No unsupported effects: `HASTE` affects allies; `HEAL` restores living allies;
  `FORTRESS_SHIELD` protects a fortress; `CATAPULT_LOCK` disables an enemy
  siege engine; `SLOWING_FIELD` slows enemies; `VAMPIRIC_BANNER` and
  `SIEGE_FRENZY` affect allied forces; `BERSERKER` depicts a Defender.
- These images are presentation assets only. Do not imply that `CastSpell`
  gameplay is implemented.

MUST-HAVE VALIDATION BEFORE DELIVERY

- Verify exactly 11 files exist and filenames match the list exactly.
- Verify every file is a valid PNG at exactly 512 x 384 pixels.
- Open every image and confirm the depicted effect matches its listed spell.
- Confirm no text, UI, watermark, unintended cropping, wrong unit, or
  unsupported effect appears.
- Compare all images as a set for consistent scale, lighting, contrast, and
  visual style.
- Reject/regenerate any failed image. Show previews only after all checks pass.
- Do not copy any image into Android resources until the user accepts the
  validated previews.

NEGATIVE PROMPT

text, letters, words, numbers, UI, HUD, card frame, border, selected outline,
check mark, lock icon, coin, price, stock count, logo, watermark, signature,
contact sheet, collage, sprite sheet, atlas, multiple spell effects in one
image, invented units, invented ammunition, invented spells, FIRE STRIKE,
WIND BLAST, EARTH SHIELD, gore, blood, photorealistic device screenshot,
low-contrast focal subject, unreadable tiny details, clipped subject, wrong
spell effect, duplicate composition, unrelated franchise, unrelated art style
